{"step_index":48,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T22:44:38Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-17T04:14:38+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-17T04:14:38+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/.gemini/antigravity/brain/39f7a808-f326-4999-9a66-c185c6afbf59/.system_generated/steps/46/content.md`\nTotal Lines: 113\nTotal Bytes: 6323\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: Title: Live Content\n2: \n3: Description: Fetched live\n4: \n5: Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/geekyutao/Inpaint-Anything/main/README.md\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: <p align=\"center\">\n10:   <img src=\"./example/IAM.png\">\n11: </p>\n12: \n13: # Inpaint Anything: Segment Anything Meets Image Inpainting\n14: Inpaint Anything can inpaint anything in **images**, **videos** and **3D scenes**!\n15: - Authors: Tao Yu, Runseng Feng, Ruoyu Feng, Jinming Liu, Xin Jin, Wenjun Zeng and Zhibo Chen.\n16: - Institutes: University of Science and Technology of China; Eastern Institute for Advanced Study.\n17: - [[Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06790)] [[Website](https://huggingface.co/spaces/InpaintAI/Inpaint-Anything)] [[Hugging Face Homepage](https://huggingface.co/InpaintAI)]\n18: <p align=\"center\">\n19:   <img src=\"./example/MainFramework.png\" width=\"100%\">\n20: </p>\n21: \n22: TL; DR: Users can select any object in an image by clicking on it. With powerful vision models, e.g., [SAM](https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.02643), [LaMa](https://arxiv.org/abs/2109.07161) and [Stable Diffusion (SD)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.10752), **Inpaint Anything** is able to remove the object smoothly (i.e., *Remove Anything*). Further, prompted by user input text, Inpaint Anything can fill the object with any desired content (i.e., *Fill Anything*) or replace the background of it arbitrarily (i.e., *Replace Anything*).\n23: \n24: ---\n25: \n26: ## 🚧 New: [`main_2026`](https://github.com/geekyutao/Inpaint-Anything/tree/main_2026) branch — modernized stack + robotics support (beta)\n27: \n28: The [**`main_2026`**](https://github.com/geekyutao/Inpaint-Anything/tree/main_2026)\n29: branch brings Inpaint Anything up to date with the 2026 model landscape, and adds\n30: a new direction: **data engineering for robotics**.\n31: \n32: | | `main` (this branch) | [`main_2026`](https://github.com/geekyutao/Inpaint-Anything/tree/main_2026) |\n33: | --- | --- | --- |\n34: | Segmentation | SAM 1 | **SAM 3** — plus open-vocabulary *text* prompts |\n35: | Video / 3D tracking | OSTrack | **SAM 3 video predictor** — one less model and checkpoint |\n36: | Video inpainting | STTN | **ProPainter** |\n37: | Text-guided fill / replace | SD 2 *(no longer downloadable)* | **SDXL**, optional **FLUX.1-Fill** |\n38: | Robotics | — | **`remove_hands.py`** — batch hand removal for Human-to-Robot pipelines |\n39: \n40: Two things you can do there that you cannot do here:\n41: \n42: - **Name the object instead of clicking it.** `--text_select \"dog\"` finds every match, which also means the pipelines can run unattended over a whole dataset.\n43: - **Prepare egocentric data for robot learning.** `remove_hands.py` erases human hands from egocentric video and exports the masks — the *hand removal and inpainting* stage of Human-to-Robot synthesis pipelines such as [Qwen-RobotManip](https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen-RobotManip) and [EgoEngine](https://egoengine.github.io/). On EgoMimic footage it matches human annotation at IoU 0.96, and it reconstructs the background rather than blacking the arm out.\n44: \n45: ```bash\n46: git checkout main_2026\n47: # then follow the Quick start in that branch's README\n48: ```\n49: \n50: > ⚠️ **`main_2026` is in beta.** It needs Python ≥ 3.12, PyTorch ≥ 2.7 and\n51: > CUDA ≥ 12.6 (SAM 3's floor), and the NeRF-based 3D path has not been\n52: > end-to-end verified on that stack yet. Every legacy backend\n53: > (SAM 1 / MobileSAM, OSTrack, STTN) is still selectable by flag, so you can fall\n54: > back per stage.\n55: >\n56: > 🤝 **Contributions very welcome** — especially on the robotics side. Issues and\n57: > PRs against `main_2026` are appreciated: more egocentric datasets, action\n58: > retargeting, robot rendering and compositing, or newer inpainting backends.\n59: > Please open an issue if you hit anything.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 📜 News\n64: [2026/7/28] <span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span> [**`main_2026`**](https://github.com/geekyutao/Inpaint-Anything/tree/main_2026) **branch (beta):** upgraded to [SAM 3](https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3) with text prompts, [ProPainter](https://github.com/sczhou/ProPainter) for video, SDXL/FLUX for text-guided editing, and **robotics support** via `remove_hands.py`. OSTrack is no longer needed. Contributions welcome!\\\n65: [2023/9/15] [Remove Anything 3D](#remove-anything-3d) code is available!\\\n66: [2023/4/30] [Remove Anything Video](#remove-anything-video) available! You can remove any object from a video!\\\n67: [2023/4/24] [Local web UI](./app) supported! You can run the demo website locally!\\\n68: [2023/4/22] [Website](https://huggingface.co/spaces/InpaintAI/Inpaint-Anything) available! You can experience Inpaint Anything through the interface!\\\n69: [2023/4/22] [Remove Anything 3D](#remove-anything-3d) available! You can remove any 3D object from a 3D scene!\\\n70: [2023/4/13] [Technical report on arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06790) available!\n71: \n72: ## 🌟 Features\n73: - [x] [**Remove** Anything](#remove-anything)\n74: - [x] [**Fill** Anything](#fill-anything)\n75: - [x] [**Replace** Anything](#replace-anything)\n76: - [x] [Remove Anything **3D**](#remove-anything-3d) (<span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span>)\n77: - [ ] Fill Anything **3D**\n78: - [ ] Replace Anything **3D**\n79: - [x] [Remove Anything **Video**](#remove-anything-video) (<span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span>)\n80: - [ ] Fill Anything **Video**\n81: - [ ] Replace Anything **Video**\n82: \n83: \n84: ## 💡 Highlights\n85: - [x] Any aspect ratio supported\n86: - [x] 2K resolution supported\n87: - [x] [Technical report on arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.06790) available (<span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span>)\n88: - [x] [Website](https://huggingface.co/spaces/InpaintAI/Inpaint-Anything) available (<span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span>)\n89: - [x] [Local web UI](./app) available (<span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span>)\n90: - [x] Multiple modalities (i.e., image, video and 3D scene) supported (<span style=\"color:red\">🔥NEW</span>)\n91: \n92: <!-- ## Updates\n93: | Date | News |\n94: | ------ | --------\n95: | 2023-04-12 | Release the Fill Anything feature | \n96: | 2023-04-10 | Release the Remove Anything feature |\n97: | 2023-04-10 | Release the first version of Inpaint Anything | -->\n98: \n99: ## <span id=\"remove-anything\">📌 Remove Anything</span>\n100: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
